        "id": 105275,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-05-28T16:08:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Medic-Tank\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/medic-tank/48/2107_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Medic-Tank:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This is mostly a question of timing. In advanced mode Voss gets an extra card play at the end of turn. This of course becomes start of turn with Sub-Zero Atmosphere. Thus when it played a forced deployment it triggered immediatly since it was start of turn. if there was ten minion in the trash would that mean:A: immediate defeat because you've been overrunned or:B: has the condition already been checked meaning he simply doesn't flip back and immediatly win at that point since it was already checked up and false when it checked up</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Voss's win condition, because it is a Start/End turn effect and in play before Forced Deployment, gets checked first. It doesn't re-check until the next round.</p>",
